    "id": "v2-383dbf-p4-practice-slot-1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Ava is 9 and her grandfather is 63. When will Ava be one-quarter of her grandfather's age?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "In 9 years.",
      "worked": "Let this happen in $x$ years.\n$$\\begin{align*}9+x&=\\frac{1}{4}(63+x)\\\\36+4x&=63+x\\\\4x-x&=63-36\\\\3x&=27\\\\x&=9\\end{align*}$$\nMultiply both sides of the first equation by 4 to obtain the second equation.\nIn 9 years.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
